stical data on users' behaviour on the website. Used for internal analytics by the website operator. — FPLC This FPLC cookie is the cross-domain linker cookie hashed from the FPID cookie. It’s not HttpOnly, which means it can be read with JavaScript. It has a relatively short lifetime, just 20 hours. — *__ga_* Keeps track of your current visit for one specific Google Analytics property. — *__ga Identifies your browser so Google Analytics can tell returning visitors from new ones. — *_FPID Identifies returning visitors so Google Analytics can report on visit patterns over time. 2 years *_FPLC Helps Google Analytics keep a consistent visitor identifier when you move between this site's subdomains or linked domains. 20 hours Hotjar Hotjar _hjSessionUser_* Stores a random ID that lets Hotjar recognise you when you return to the site. 1 year _hjSession_* Links the pages you view during one visit to the same Hotjar session. 30 minutes Marketing & Social Media These cookies and similar technologies help advertising and social media partners personalise your experience, show you relevant ads, measure campaign results, and enable sharing features. Google Google Ads _gcl_au Identifies your browser so Google can link a later purchase or sign-up on this site to the adverts you saw or clicked. 90 days IDE Recognises your browser so Google can measure how adverts perform and show you adverts that fit your interests. 13 months _gcl_ls This item is used by Google Ads to store advertising click identifiers for conversion measurement. When visitors do not accept tracking cookies, Google can send a cookieless ping via Consent Mode v2 with anonymized data to measure conversions and advertising performance. Data may be stored temporarily or persistently, depending on the implementation. — Google NID Lets Google remember your preferences and helps it choose which adverts to show you. 6 months __Secure-ENID Remembers your Google preferences, such as language, and can be used to choose which adverts you see. 13 months eur.nl Website FPAU Identifies your browser so Google can link a later purchase or sign-up on this site to the adverts you saw or clicked. 90 days *__fbp Stores a Meta (Facebook) browser identifier so visits and conversions can be attributed back to Meta advertising. — *__gcl_au Identifies your browser so Google can link a later purchase or sign-up on this site to the adverts you saw or clicked. 90 days *_FPAU Identifies your browser so Google can link a later purchase or sign-up on this site to the adverts you saw or clicked. 90 days LinkedIn LinkedIn lidc Helps LinkedIn choose which of its data centres handles your browser's requests. 1 day bcookie Identifies your browser to LinkedIn when LinkedIn content or advertising is loaded on this site. 1 year li_gc Remembers whether you agreed to LinkedIn's non-essential cookies as a visitor without a LinkedIn account. 6 months Meta Meta Pixel _fbp Identifies your browser to Meta, so your visits to this site can be used for advertising on Facebook and Instagram and to measure how adverts perform. 90 days lastExternalReferrer Detects how the user reached the website by registering their last URL-address — lastExternalReferrerTime Detects how the user reached the website by registering their last URL-address — Consent dialog opened"
